--unwind 5

^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
A callable bound to different functions across if/else branches now
dispatches path-sensitively via a runtime tag, so pick(True) calls af
(==1) and pick(False) calls bf (==2); likewise op with add/sub and
arguments. Previously the last-processed branch won unconditionally
(differential §10), making pick(True) == 1 a false alarm and, in
general, a property depending on the other callable a missed bug.
